## 2. Confusion Matrix

The confusion matrix shows EXACTLY where your model goes wrong.

### The 4 Cells
```
                    PREDICTED
                  No        Yes
ACTUAL   No  |  TN ✅  |  FP ❌  |
         Yes |  FN ❌  |  TP ✅  |
```

| Cell | Full Name | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| TP | True Positive | Predicted YES → Actually YES ✅ |
| TN | True Negative | Predicted NO → Actually NO ✅ |
| FP | False Positive | Predicted YES → Actually NO ❌ (Type 1 Error) |
| FN | False Negative | Predicted NO → Actually YES ❌ (Type 2 Error) |

### Analogy — COVID Test 🏥
```
Test says Positive + Have COVID     = TP ✅ correct alarm
Test says Negative + No COVID       = TN ✅ correct all-clear
Test says Positive + No COVID       = FP ❌ false alarm
Test says Negative + Have COVID     = FN ❌ missed case — DANGEROUS!
```

### Code
```python
from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

y_pred = model.predict(X_test)

# Get confusion matrix
cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)
print("Confusion Matrix:")
print(cm)

# Visualize
disp = ConfusionMatrixDisplay(confusion_matrix=cm)
disp.plot()
plt.title("Confusion Matrix")
plt.show()
```

### Reading the Output
```
[[90  15]
 [22  51]]

TN=90  FP=15   ← Row 0: actual negatives
FN=22  TP=51   ← Row 1: actual positives
```

