## Interview Tips — Day 4

**Q: Why is accuracy not always a good metric?**
> *"Accuracy is misleading on imbalanced datasets. If 95% of data belongs
> to one class, a model that always predicts that class gets 95% accuracy
> without learning anything. Precision, Recall and F1 Score give a much
> more honest picture of model performance."*

**Q: What is the difference between Precision and Recall?**
> *"Precision measures how reliable the model's positive predictions are —
> out of all predicted positives, how many were actually positive.
> Recall measures coverage — out of all actual positives, how many did
> the model catch. Precision matters when false positives are costly,
> Recall matters when false negatives are costly."*

**Q: Why is Random Forest better than a single Decision Tree?**
> *"A single Decision Tree overfits easily and is sensitive to noise.
> Random Forest builds hundreds of trees, each on a random subset of
> data and features, then takes a majority vote. This averaging effect
> reduces overfitting and gives much more stable, accurate predictions."*

**Q: When would you use Logistic Regression over Random Forest?**
> *"Logistic Regression when I need interpretability, probability scores,
> or when data is linearly separable. Random Forest when I need higher
> accuracy and the interpretability is less important."*

